// SUPERSEDED CADENCE — ORGANIC FIRING (Eric, 2026-08-14,
// design/organic_firing.md delta 5): the "pure function re-applied to
// unchanged inputs is not an event" clause below is REPEALED — a
// recursive call fires per triggering delivery, so x = [1, 2, 2] now
// emits on ALL THREE cycles on both engines ([1:7 2:7 3:7]), and the
// derivation-changed machinery this header describes is deleted. The
// ruling's headline (recursion fires like the hand-inlined chain)
// survives — both now fire per delivery. Historical header follows.
// THE RULING (Eric, 2026-08-13): whether a callee is recursive is not
// observable in firing — recursion fires like the hand-inlined chain
// of distinct functions, and a pure function re-applied to unchanged
// inputs is not an event. Ground truth: the non-recursive retained
// twin (h2->h1->h0, rt_ia) is quiet on the same-value re-delivery in
// BOTH engines, shipped and unsurprising.
//
// x delivers 1, 2, 2. Cycles 1-2 fire (selection flips + fresh deeper
// levels); cycle 3 re-delivers the same 2 — every selection unchanged,
// the const base arm consumes nothing — QUIET: [1:7 2:7], no [3:7].
// Interp: unconditional transient retention (instances never park;
// the retained chain's same-arm re-matches are organically quiet).
// Kernel: the derivation-changed bit (wire slot 3) — the region-root
// call site's args memo reads unchanged scalar formals and the nomem
// selection paths dampen their becoming-selected fires to quiet.
// The pre-ruling kernel (round-6 fire-on-triggering) emitted [3:7].
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:2]); let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => i64:7, _ => i64:0 + f(n - i64:1)}; f(x)}
